{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":36,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.two_isKnownMagic_of_nonTrivialBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.two_isKnownMagic_of_nonTrivialBinding","kind":"instance","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L339-L354","doc":"**Conditional instance.** `NonTrivialBindingAtTwo q` discharges the\nn = 2 case of the per-n axiom collection for `MagicEqualsEmpirical`.\n\nThis one stays an `instance`, deliberately.  It is the §3b-cond\npattern working as intended: the `[NonTrivialBindingAtTwo q]` binder\n*is* the dependency edge, and `is_prime` is a real derivation —\n`two_isAlgebraicallyPrime` combines `decomp_two_eq_oneOne` (proved\narithmetic) with the class field.  It looked vacuous only because\n§11 used to supply `NonTrivialBindingAtTwo q` globally, so\nresolution chained through and answered `IsKnownMagic 2 q`\nunconditionally.  With §11 gone the chain has no free end. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.two_isAlgebraicallyPrime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.two_isAlgebraicallyPrime","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L319-L337","doc":"**Theorem.** Under `NonTrivialBindingAtTwo q`, `n = 2` is\nalgebraically prime at `q`. The proof:\n\n1. Any non-trivial decomposition of 2 is `[1, 1]` (proved\n   arithmetic, `decomp_two_eq_oneOne`).\n2. `ψ_2(q) ∉ tensor-span([1, 1])` is the typeclass axiom.\n\nCombining: the universal-quantifier in `IsAlgebraicallyPrime 2 q`\nreduces to a single check, which the typeclass provides. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.NonTrivialBindingAtTwo.not_in_oneOne_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.NonTrivialBindingAtTwo.not_in_oneOne_span","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L316-L316","doc":"ψ_2(q) is not in the tensor span via decomposition [1, 1]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.NonTrivialBindingAtTwo.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.NonTrivialBindingAtTwo.mk","kind":"ctor","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L314-L314","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.NonTrivialBindingAtTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.NonTrivialBindingAtTwo","kind":"class","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L303-L317","doc":"**Typeclass (n = 2 binding axiom).** The single non-trivial axiom\nneeded to discharge `IsKnownMagic 2 q`: at substrate `q`, the\ncanonical state `ψ_2(q)` is **not** in the closed tensor span of\n`ψ_1 ⊗ ψ_1` (the unique non-trivial decomposition of 2).\n\nThis is the minimal axiom — by `decomp_two_eq_oneOne`, proving\nprimality at n = 2 reduces to this single check.\n\nIn framework language: the SDP at n = 2 produces a *non-trivial\nbound state*, distinct from two free single-strands. Empirically\nexpected at any reasonable substrate `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.decomp_two_eq_oneOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.decomp_two_eq_oneOne","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L282-L301","doc":"**Lemma (decomposition of 2).** The only non-trivial decomposition\nof `n = 2` (length ≥ 2, all entries ≥ 1) is `[1, 1]`. Provable\nby elementary arithmetic via `sum_ge_length_of_all_pos`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.one_in_ladder_is_known","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.one_in_ladder_is_known","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L272-L278","doc":"**Corollary.** The `n = 1` constraint of the conjecture\n`MagicEqualsEmpirical` is automatically satisfied — it is not a\nfree axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.magicEqualsEmpirical_of_perNAxioms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.magicEqualsEmpirical_of_perNAxioms","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L241-L270","doc":"**Theorem (assembly).** Suppose we have, at substrate `q`:\n- For every `n ∈ empiricalMagicLadder`, an `IsKnownMagic n q`\n  instance.\n- For every `n ∉ empiricalMagicLadder`, an `IsKnownNotMagic n q`\n  instance.\n\nThen the conjecture `MagicEqualsEmpirical` holds at `q`.\n\nThis is the *structural* conjecture: it factors the iff into\nper-n axioms. The `n = 1` axiom is **discharged** by the\nproved `one_isKnownMagic` instance; the others (n in {2, 8, 20,\n28, 50, 82, 126} and n outside the ladder) remain conjectural,\nwaiting for the SDP machinery.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.empirical_of_prime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.empirical_of_prime","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L230-L237","doc":"Re-export reverse direction: if `n` is algebraically prime at\n`q_0`, then `n` lies on the empirical magic ladder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.prime_at_empirical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.prime_at_empirical","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L221-L228","doc":"Re-export forward direction: at `n` on the empirical ladder,\n`n` is algebraically prime at `q_0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.MagicEqualsEmpirical.prime_iff_in_ladder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.MagicEqualsEmpirical.prime_iff_in_ladder","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L216-L216","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.MagicEqualsEmpirical.q_0_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.MagicEqualsEmpirical.q_0_pos","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L215-L215","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.MagicEqualsEmpirical.q_0_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.MagicEqualsEmpirical.q_0_value","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L214-L214","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.MagicEqualsEmpirical.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.MagicEqualsEmpirical.mk","kind":"ctor","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L213-L213","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.MagicEqualsEmpirical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.MagicEqualsEmpirical","kind":"class","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L205-L219","doc":"**Conjecture (`conj:algebraic-primality-equals-empirical-at-q0`).**\nAt substrate `q = q_0` (the framework's distinguished substrate\nvalue), the set of algebraically-prime integers equals the\nempirical magic ladder.\n\nConcrete instances supply the substrate value `q_0_value` and\nthe iff. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.empiricalMagicLadder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.empiricalMagicLadder","kind":"def","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L201-L203","doc":"The empirical magic ladder `{1, 2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.zero_isKnownNotMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.zero_isKnownNotMagic","kind":"instance","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L193-L197","doc":"**Proved instance.** For every `q`, `n = 0` is known to be\nnon-magic — by the `n ≥ 1` clause of the definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.one_isKnownMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.one_isKnownMagic","kind":"instance","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L185-L191","doc":"**Proved instance.** For every `q : ℝ`, `n = 1` is known to be\nmagic at `q` — discharged by `one_isAlgebraicallyPrime`.\nNo additional axioms required; the proof is structural\n(vacuous primality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsKnownNotMagic.not_prime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsKnownNotMagic.not_prime","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L183-L183","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsKnownNotMagic.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsKnownNotMagic.mk","kind":"ctor","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L182-L182","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsKnownNotMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsKnownNotMagic","kind":"class","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L181-L183","doc":"Per-n assertion that `n` is *known* to be non-magic at `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsKnownMagic.is_prime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsKnownMagic.is_prime","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L179-L179","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsKnownMagic.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsKnownMagic.mk","kind":"ctor","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L178-L178","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsKnownMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsKnownMagic","kind":"class","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L175-L179","doc":"Per-n assertion that `n` is *known* to be magic at `q`.\nUsed to factorise the empirical-match conjecture into per-n\npropositions, each of which can be discharged independently. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.zero_not_isAlgebraicallyPrime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.zero_not_isAlgebraicallyPrime","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L165-L171","doc":"**Lemma (decomposability of n = 0).** Zero is *not* algebraically\nprime: it fails the `n ≥ 1` clause of the definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.not_prime_of_inTensorSpan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.not_prime_of_inTensorSpan","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L150-L163","doc":"**Lemma (decomposability negates primality).** If for some\nnon-trivial decomposition `decomp` of `n`, the canonical state\n`canonicalState n q` lies in the indicated tensor span, then\n`n` is *not* algebraically prime at `q`. Direct unfolding of the\ndefinition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.one_isAlgebraicallyPrime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.one_isAlgebraicallyPrime","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L127-L146","doc":"**Theorem (`prop:n-equals-1-vacuous-magic`).** For every `q : ℝ`,\nthe integer `n = 1` is algebraically prime — vacuously, because\nno decomposition into `k ≥ 2` parts each `≥ 1` can sum to `1`.\n\nThe proof needs only elementary arithmetic: a list of length ≥ 2\nwith all entries ≥ 1 has sum ≥ 2 > 1, contradicting `sum = 1`.\nNo SDP / Hecke / tensor-product analysis is invoked. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:n-equals-1-vacuous-magic","label":"prop:n-equals-1-vacuous-magic","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/n-equals-1-vacuous-magic.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.sum_ge_length_of_all_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.sum_ge_length_of_all_pos","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L109-L123","doc":"**Lemma (sum dominates length under positivity).** For any list\nof natural numbers with every entry `≥ 1`, the sum is at least\nthe length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsAlgebraicallyPrime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.IsAlgebraicallyPrime","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L90-L105","doc":"**Definition (algebraic primality).** A natural number `n ≥ 1`\nis **algebraically prime** at substrate `q` if and only if\n`canonicalState n q` is *not* in the closed span of any\nnon-trivial tensor-product decomposition.\n\nConventions:\n- `n = 0` is *not* prime (vacuum).\n- `n = 1` is prime *vacuously* — no non-trivial decomposition\n  exists.\n- For `n ≥ 2`, primality is non-trivial. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:algebraic-primality","label":"def:algebraic-primality","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/algebraic-primality.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.NonTrivialDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.NonTrivialDecomposition","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L83-L86","doc":"A *non-trivial* decomposition of `n`: a list of length ≥ 2,\nall entries ≥ 1, summing to `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.InTensorSpan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.InTensorSpan","kind":"opaque","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L54-L79","doc":"The \"is in the closed span of tensor products of canonical states\nindexed by a decomposition\" predicate.  **`opaque` since\n2026-08-24**; the genuine span predicate is still the upgrade\ntarget.\n\nIt was `def … : Prop := False`, ignoring all four of its arguments.\nIts own docstring drew the consequence — *\"every `n ≥ 1` is\ntherefore algebraically prime\"* — and stopped there.  That\nconsequence is not a harmless simplification; it is the negation of\nwhat this file exists to state.  `IsAlgebraicallyPrime n q` unfolded\nto `n ≥ 1 ∧ ∀ decomp, … → ¬False`, i.e. definitionally to `n ≥ 1`.\nSo `IsKnownMagic n q` was provable in one line for **every** `n ≥ 1`,\nmagic or not, and `IsKnownNotMagic n q` was *unprovable* for every\n`n ≥ 1` — while `MagicEqualsEmpirical` asserts primality holds\nexactly on `{2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126}` and\n`magicEqualsEmpirical_of_perNAxioms` needs both halves.  The model\ndid not under-specify the conjecture; it contradicted it.\n\nSealing the body keeps the type and every structural result that\nquantifies over the predicate (`IsAlgebraicallyPrime`,\n`not_prime_of_inTensorSpan`, `two_isAlgebraicallyPrime`) while\nremoving the ability to discharge a primality claim by unfolding.\nSame remedy, and the same reason, as the three `opaque` surreal\nplaceholders in `QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.canonicalState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.canonicalState","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L48-L52","doc":"The canonical confinement-SDP optimum state `ψ_n(q)`.\nConcrete model: a record pinning `strands := n`, `qVal := q`\n(the canonical observable assignment). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.SDPState.qVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.SDPState.qVal","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Substrate parameter `q` at which the SDP is evaluated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.SDPState.strands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.SDPState.strands","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Strand count `n` (recorded for downstream decomposition checks). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.SDPState.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.SDPState.mk","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.SDPState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.SDPState","kind":"structure","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/AlgebraicPrimality.lean#L39-L46","doc":"Surrogate type for the state space of an `n`-strand hadron at\nsubstrate `q`. Concrete model: a record carrying the strand\ncount and substrate parameter as observable fields. ","signatureChunk":0}]}